+# Incremental track-editor preparation — 2026-10-18
+
+EIP01 caches road-section work and finished spatial uploads. EIP02 warms the selected reusable prop before placement. EIP03 budgets completed mesh installation across frames. EIP04 prepares the selected biome's rendering before canvas input opens. G01/R01/Q01 preserve canonical driving, existing documents, saving/history, bounded caches and reproducible local verification.
+
+Road preparation now retains immutable per-piece work, clipping fragments, normalized tile streams and locally sampled Desert deformation. Section identities include the actual sampled section, endpoint neighbours, exposed crossing contours, connected Desert wear phases and relevant road cells. Index changes after inserting a distant piece rebind the current ownership/phase indices. Existing snow-deposit and sand-chip limits retain their original ordered arbitration; cached work is reused only when the remaining capacity and nearby occupancy permit the same result. Cancellation cannot admit partially generated section results.
+
+Whole triangles are grouped into 32 m upload tiles, with the existing 16 m Night light tiles, and at most 12,288 vertices per upload. Vertex attributes and normals remain exact. Unchanged immutable GPU meshes are borrowed from existing scene/cache resources; new materials bind the current masks and extent. In the four-piece regression, widening the crossing's first road rebuilds three affected pieces and retains the distant fourth. Pine retains 12 of 22 finished mesh sections; Desert retains 27 of 45. These are work counts on a small fixture, not a whole-editor latency or phone claim. Global topology, union traversal, kerb preparation and ordered decoration bookkeeping still run; connected UV changes can legitimately invalidate an entire connected component.
+
+Intermediate sections share the existing 32 MiB CPU/GPU road allowance. Their own ceiling is half that allowance, rather than an additional allocation. Role limits and eviction priority prevent thousands of small scalar clipping fragments displacing reusable piece work. Existing road/world/disk and prop cache limits remain. Larger uncached work still falls back to a complete, cancellable preparation.
+
+Selecting a prop or changing container paint queues one background preparation using the original reusable model cache and exact model key. Rapid selections coalesce. The default selection also warms during editor preparation. Cache access is synchronized with the worker. An immediate placement records the document first; a cold model is no longer built synchronously in that placement handler. Preview generations prevent superseded delayed work replacing the current document. The existing inexpensive tyre-only update remains immediate.
+
+Road uploads, large baked prop assemblies and completed Desert terrain/prop deformation share a per-visual frame allowance: at most 24,576 requested vertices, with a cooperative 4 ms installation target. Concurrent resumptions cannot reset another installer's allowance. Large assemblies and deformation split their CPU arrays on the worker, then upload bounded surfaces on main. Superseded prop work checks its identity again after a yield and before publishing. Empty clipped surfaces are skipped. The old scene and immediate canvas overlay remain available during replacement. Individual driver calls are atomic; this is not a hard bound on GPU/driver or total frame time.
+
+Before editing, a small representative road/curve/bridge fixture prepares biome materials. The receiving renderer's MSAA, environment, sun, fog and material next passes are used for the preparation draws. The actual completed editor view is also submitted before canvas input opens. Reapplying an unchanged biome no longer replaces Winter's already-prepared sky. Mobile receives actual mesh/surface pipeline evidence; Compatibility renders representative materials in the frustum. This follows [Godot's pipeline-compilation guidance](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.html). Later unseen combinations, driver changes and shader specialization remain possible; no general elimination of shader stalls is claimed.
+
+Runtime files are `game/core/app.gd`, `game/editor/editor_canvas.gd`, `editor_world.gd`, `road_preparation.gd`, `road_piece_work.gd`, `road_sections.gd`, `material_preparation.gd`, `placed_object_batches.gd`, and `game/track/native_track_visual.gd`, `creator_prop_visual.gd`, `desert_road_relief.gd`, `shoulder_mesh.gd`. Tests are `test_editor_preparation.gd`, the existing placement regression and App fixture. The App gesture fixture waits for actual preparation instead of two frames. Placement fixtures use currently permitted biome props and can write evidence to a separate requested directory. Existing gesture, geometry, collision, save and history assertions remain.
+
+The new regression compares final engine-encoded triangle multisets against the independent uncached builder in all five biomes. It exercises crossings/joins, distant insertion/reindexing, connected Desert UV changes, mid-build cancellation, bounded caches, actual upload yielding, rapid prop selection/teardown and large sliced prop geometry. Native checks compare the complete editor pixels. Static wind is evaluated at one shared time only in the comparison fixture. Both scenes submit their pipelines and compilation counters settle before byte-exact capture, so moving grass or an initial ubershader is not compared with a later specialized draw. Production shaders, wind, MSAA and pixel assertions are unchanged.
+
+Completed validation and actual command receipts are recorded in [the evidence directory](evidence/editor-preparation-2026-10-18/). Final test totals are in the renderer/headless JSON reports and [test receipts](evidence/editor-preparation-2026-10-18/test-receipts.json). Focused preparation 270 GDScript-fallback, 280 Compatibility and 280 desktop Mobile checks pass. App 141, editor workflow 252, placement 205, road cache 70 and whole-project parser 890 checks pass. The placement run preceded the final initial-view warmup and empty-upload guard; the final App/workflow/render checks exercise those changes. Desktop renderer runs use the RTX 3090, not an Android device. Timing rows came from shared desktop processes and are not paired performance measurements.
+
